{
  "id": "Compound::DB01162 - Gene::146",
  "verbalization": "Terazosin, a selective alpha-1 adrenergic receptor antagonist, is shown to bind to Adra1b and Adra1a, both of which are involved in the Alpha-adrenergic Receptor Activity. This activity is further linked to Adra1d, suggesting a potential role for Terazosin in modulating the function of Adra1d. The evidence from the three paths indicates a consistent mechanism where Terazosin interacts with alpha-adrenergic receptors, which are implicated in the function of Adra1d. The high scores in the final scores suggest a strong and reliable interaction, supported by multiple pathways. The mechanism appears to be centered on the inhibition of alpha-adrenergic receptor activity, which could influence the function of Adra1d in physiological processes. The integration of these pathways supports the hypothesis that Terazosin may exert its effects on Adra1d through the modulation of alpha-adrenergic receptor activity.",
